# Trivy ignore list for base-image (python:3.14-slim / Debian trixie) OS
# package CVEs whose fixed +deb13uN builds are ASSIGNED in the Debian security
# tracker (so Trivy's DB reports "Fixed Version: ...") but are NOT yet published
# to the trixie / trixie-security apt mirror. The runtime stage already runs
# `apt-get install --only-upgrade <pkg>=<glob>` for each of these packages, but
# the glob matches only the currently-installed (still-vulnerable) build, so the
# upgrade is a no-op until Debian actually pushes the patched .deb. Once the
# fixed builds land in the mirror, the apt --only-upgrade lines in the Dockerfile
# pull them automatically and these entries become redundant (revisit on the
# next base-image digest bump).
#
# justification: fixed package build not yet available in the Debian trixie apt
# mirror; upgrade is applied automatically once published. Base-image debt, not
# a code vulnerability in this component.

